Umbriel's background-frame tick runs only while a window needs it (gemini-pda-mainline, MIT).

Upstream-ready message:

  server: arm the background-frame tick only while a window needs it

  The 100 ms background-frame tick sends frame callbacks to mapped
  toplevels that are off the rendered scene but cannot be suspended (X11
  windows, xdg clients older than v6) and to suspended ones that still
  owe a commit for a configure. It re-armed itself unconditionally, so
  the compositor woke ten times a second even when no window qualified,
  including with every output powered off.

  Arm it only when a view qualifies: after the suspension sync, which
  already runs on every scene visibility, map, capture and overview
  change, and after a configure is sent to a toplevel, which can leave a
  suspended hidden view owing a commit. The tick stops itself once
  nothing qualifies.

  On a battery device with an idle desktop and the output blanked, this
  removes about 10 wakeups/s.

Measured on a Gemini PDA (custodian census, 2026-11-13): 1198 timerfd arms in 120 s with the
output off, all from this tick.

